From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:53:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ag71xx: accept all RGMII modes

The RGMII MACs only list PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII as supported, so
phylink refuses rgmii-id, rgmii-rxid and rgmii-txid, which boards use
when the PHY adds the RGMII delays. The MAC does not care which side
adds them, so accept all of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c
@@ -1173,8 +1173,7 @@ static int ag71xx_phylink_setup(struct a
 
 	if ((ag71xx_is(ag, AR9340) && ag->mac_idx == 0) ||
 	    ag71xx_is(ag, QCA9550))
-		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII,
-			  ag->phylink_config.supported_interfaces);
+		phy_interface_set_rgmii(ag->phylink_config.supported_interfaces);
 
 	phylink = phylink_create(&ag->phylink_config, ag->pdev->dev.fwnode,
 				 ag->phy_if_mode, &ag71xx_phylink_mac_ops);
